Patch Set 9:

(2 comments)

AI code review results below, please doublecheck

Looks good. One optional documentation fix inline, for whenever the patch is next refreshed; no need to re-spin for it alone.

On test coverage: sanity-flr test_213a checks ioctl argument validation and the SET_MIRROR alias (through `lfs mirror resync`), but it never does I/O on an FLR file through LL_IOC_SET_IO_SCOPE itself. io_scope also always opens with O_DIRECT. So these paths have no coverage:
- a MIRROR-scope read or write landing on the chosen mirror;
- -ESTALE on a write when a non-zero ios_layout_version doesn't match lcm_layout_gen;
- -EINVAL for a MIRROR scope on a fd opened without O_DIRECT;
- -EINVAL for non-zero ios_flags, ios_padding, or identity fields;
- llapi_io_scope_clear(), and SET_MIRROR(0) on a fd opened without O_DIRECT.
If the patch is refreshed, could io_scope get a flag that skips O_DIRECT, and could test_213a do a `-w` write on the mirrored file with a matching and a stale `-v`?
